{"lines":[{"t":"Audioscripts","c":1,"h":0.015310230979747486,"y":0.070227584390257114,"w":0.111328976949056,"x":0.14639992225116624},{"w":0.67676981608072917,"c":1,"h":0.015619828174441186,"t":"ALICE: I know. I'd at least have expected them to contain a small percentage of real chicken.","x":0.1465703027613976,"y":0.11521458537773088},{"h":0.014875986771052396,"c":1,"t":":Absolutely.","y":0.13185594967277403,"x":0.18022771657439429,"w":0.10207232157389323},{"c":1,"h":0.014534883321060788,"t":"ALICE: I think having nutritional food labeling has been a good idea, don't you? I think it will","x":0.14661655167677964,"y":0.14680232577727004,"w":0.66541351318359376},{"x":0.19736842709611552,"w":0.61654134114583337,"y":0.16279069787163147,"h":0.014607885769698514,"c":1,"t":"change people's behaviour and stop mothers, in particular, buying the wrong things."},{"x":0.18978745252090165,"c":1,"t":"But didn't that study kind of prove the opposite? People didn't necessarily stop buying","y":0.17610509776139627,"w":0.63548400878906242,"h":0.018509550395506169},{"c":1,"t":"unhealthy products.","x":0.19736841813853848,"h":0.013217104379392275,"y":0.19476744190237838,"w":0.14849624633789063},{"x":0.14654649023802041,"w":0.6636718241373698,"h":0.017161254489797884,"t":"ALICE: They only said that might be the case. Those findings weren't that conclusive and it","y":0.2078042697190261,"c":1},{"y":0.22529069758623699,"w":0.5,"x":0.19924812021685112,"c":1,"t":"was quite a small-scale study. I think more research has to be done.","h":0.011670023567509236},{"x":0.195393907852627,"c":1,"y":0.23934641416407654,"w":0.24458567301432288,"h":0.016757481188752643,"t":"Yes, I think you're probably right."},{"x":0.14839665289828882,"y":0.27756411150790705,"h":0.017572253731397924,"w":0.3780301920572916,"c":1,"t":"JACK: What do you think of the traffic-light system?"},{"w":0.66369593302408847,"t":"ALICE: I think supermarkets like the idea of having a colour-coded system - red, orange or","c":1,"h":0.018605970983265774,"x":0.1465370061094696,"y":0.29251074323142523},{"h":0.01566130962973622,"y":0.30850949664517957,"c":1,"x":0.19916394073158331,"w":0.37797996520996091,"t":"green - for levels of fat, sugar and salt in a product."},{"t":"But it's not been adopted universally. And not on all products. Why do you suppose","w":0.62030075073242186,"x":0.1860902271982359,"h":0.015988371407532731,"y":0.32412790726238816,"c":1},{"c":1,"y":0.35608499694878204,"w":0.63157892862955722,"x":0.1466165506432596,"t":"ALICE: Pressure from the food manufacturers. Hardly surprising that some of them are","h":0.01455453773198867},{"w":0.41917292277018231,"t":"opposed to flagging up how unhealthy their products are.","c":1,"x":0.19924812500164185,"h":0.014577936220384058,"y":0.37209302345105999},{"c":1,"x":0.19543171572260329,"t":"I'd have thought it would have been compulsory. It seems ridiculous it isn't.","y":0.38625046548578434,"w":0.55086578369140626,"h":0.016724377697848181},{"y":0.40261627926257715,"t":"I know. And what I couldn't get over is the fact that it was brought in without enough","x":0.19548872803573733,"c":1,"w":0.61654134114583337,"h":0.014640642916549873},{"x":0.19914314769633043,"y":0.41709391657582873,"t":"consultation - a lot of experts had deep reservations about it.","w":0.4475780232747395,"h":0.017518104312501226,"c":1},{"y":0.43749999991151056,"h":0.0087209303610875644,"w":0.035714286168416348,"x":0.14849624028567487,"c":1,"t":"JACK:"},{"y":0.43288679550260256,"x":0.19732747901907904,"w":0.61100229899088543,"h":0.017452260255045982,"c":1,"t":"That is a bit weird. I suppose there's an argument for doing the research now when"},{"h":0.015548534110831347,"w":0.29532099405924478,"c":1,"t":"consumers are familiar with this system.","x":0.20104031970433028,"y":0.44841836904257071},{"c":1,"x":0.14661653968756733,"t":"ALICE: Yeah, maybe.","h":0.014600398228848621,"y":0.46511627914857812,"w":0.15601504007975259},{"w":0.57904047648111978,"t":"The participants in the survey were quite positive about the traffic-light system.","y":0.47925927475732433,"x":0.19731378075741779,"h":0.016663640372920563,"c":1},{"c":1,"w":0.043233083089192686,"y":0.49854651139687189,"x":0.14661654113867434,"t":"ALICE:","h":0.011627907148116789},{"y":0.49549259492840825,"w":0.61654134114583325,"t":"Mmm. But I don't think they targeted the right people. They should have focused on","h":0.01481004507405026,"c":1,"x":0.19548872797794767},{"x":0.19913026347612231,"c":1,"w":0.62052408854166674,"y":0.50932186966116899,"t":"people with low literacy levels because these labels are designed to be accessible to","h":0.01916639987530433},{"c":1,"t":"Yeah. But it's good to get feedback from all socio-economic groups. And there wasn't","x":0.19736842599738358,"y":0.54215116298686694,"w":0.62593983968098954,"h":0.014534883321060788},{"t":"much variation in their responses.","w":0.24812029520670575,"y":0.5595621378916652,"h":0.013200257566001294,"c":1,"x":0.1992481229890159},{"x":0.19543402227327306,"t":"No. But if they hadn't interviewed participants face-to-face, they could have used a","w":0.61287963867187489,"c":1,"h":0.017215739199214042,"y":0.57185613971125537},{"t":"much bigger sample size. I wonder why they chose that method?","y":0.5882275789530691,"w":0.47763946533203122,"x":0.19915382740876414,"h":0.016398903330295034,"c":1},{"x":0.19919995387990505,"h":0.017398533326767329,"c":1,"w":0.58094375610351556,"t":"Dunno. How were they selected? Did they volunteer or were they approached?","y":0.60315987225135814},{"c":1,"w":0.59035863240559894,"x":0.19731135559837346,"t":"I think they volunteered. The thing that wasn't stated was how often they bought","y":0.61877171076798809,"h":0.017256850361133225},{"c":1,"x":0.1991630023768467,"y":0.6344897075127347,"h":0.016860417834574926,"t":"packaged food - all we know is how frequently they used the supermarket.","w":0.54715154012044276},{"x":0.15037594165543083,"t":"SECTION 4","c":1,"y":0.68604651134148364,"w":0.14097743988037109,"h":0.016142799711503786},{"w":0.66745188395182287,"y":0.71210433851002308,"h":0.017809282635690704,"c":1,"t":"In my presentation, I'm going to talk about coffee, and its importance both in economic and","x":0.14654914515145417},{"x":0.15037592794362184,"h":0.013200257566001294,"c":1,"y":0.72955569838718393,"t":"social terms. We think it was first drunk in the Arab world, but there's hardly any documentary","w":0.68045115152994784},{"h":0.018782419154356966,"c":1,"t":"evidence of it before the 1500s, although of course that doesn't mean that people didn't know","y":0.74362852218090669,"x":0.14843279911523591,"w":0.68434677124023435},{"h":0.013081395234588844,"y":0.76162790690305449,"t":"about it before then.","w":0.15037593841552732,"c":1,"x":0.14849624135614609},{"t":"However, there is evidence that coffee was originally gathered from bushes growing wild","x":0.14844029185288643,"y":0.78237178211550473,"h":0.017244297231464145,"c":1,"w":0.64861735026041667},{"c":1,"w":0.66176712036132812,"h":0.016731539773541915,"y":0.79892314549192034,"x":0.14843914713816911,"t":"in Ethiopia, in the northeast of Africa. In the early sixteenth century, it was being bought by"},{"h":0.020554850198189367,"c":1,"t":"traders, and gradually its use as a drink spread throughout the Middle East. It's also known","y":0.81129836904781805,"x":0.14833888946405693,"w":0.66757904052734374},{"t":"that in 1522, in the Turkish city of Constantinople, which was the centre of the Ottoman","w":0.63735621134440101,"x":0.14843270119517418,"y":0.82932247793886726,"h":0.01779745781106945,"c":1},{"w":0.44172932942708343,"x":0.14849623744688656,"t":"Empire, the court physician approved its use as a medicine.","h":0.016106298487184811,"c":1,"y":0.84738372065541678},{"h":0.020561729180605615,"w":0.62434890747070315,"c":1,"t":"By the mid-1500s, coffee bushes were being cultivated in the Yemen and for the next","y":0.8656524118856731,"x":0.14836370234310209},{"t":"hundred years this region produced most of the coffee drunk in Africa and the Arab world","y":0.88228029470893765,"w":0.65250473022460942,"h":0.019370916652740822,"x":0.1483663711950311,"c":1},{"t":"What's particularly interesting about coffee is its effect on social life. It was rarely drunk at","w":0.6561875406901041,"h":0.018290211443584781,"y":0.89826322732527186,"x":0.14841757284812693,"c":1},{"w":0.68443827311197913,"h":0.019735653171674361,"c":1,"x":0.1483988913232008,"y":0.91364516801290885,"t":"home, but instead people went to coffee houses to drink it. These people, usually men, would"},{"y":0.94767441865923707,"c":1,"x":0.15037594091847048,"h":0.014534883321060788,"t":"116","w":0.033834584554036456},{"h":0.014134836289012132,"w":0.086723130544026694,"t":"Q27 & Q28","y":0.32360118649358638,"x":0.84197678049838487,"c":1},{"h":0.01481004507405026,"y":0.54056664536859933,"x":0.84210526251231099,"c":1,"w":0.086466166178385429,"t":"Q29 & Q30"}],"h":3106,"w":2400}